@*
    CASE-007: finishing edit mode with unsaved changes asks first.

    Rendered by every page that carries edit mode. The script in site.js finds
    this by id and treats any form holding an editLeaseToken as the work that
    would be lost, so the two pages share one dialog rather than each keeping
    its own copy of the same three answers.
*@
<div id="edit-finish-confirm" class="reason-dialog-backdrop" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="edit-finish-title" hidden>
    <div class="reason-dialog">
        <h2 id="edit-finish-title">Save your changes before finishing?</h2>
        <p>Values not saved are not kept.</p>
        <div class="button-row">
            <button type="button" class="secondary-action" data-edit-finish-keep>Keep editing</button>
            <button type="button" class="secondary-action" data-edit-finish-discard>Discard</button>
            <button type="button" class="primary-action" data-edit-finish-save>Save changes</button>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
